  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "J. Orin Edson was an American manufacturer who founded Bayliner and made recreational boating accessible to a mass market. Starting with used craft sold from a parking lot, he integrated retail, production and packaged sales of boat, motor and trailer. Bayliner’s rapid growth and sale to Brunswick financed later investments and substantial educational philanthropy.",
